  "verbalization": "Phomalide is implicated in the biological activity of CCRF-HSB-2 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Phomalide acts as a target for SNU-387, which in turn is a target of multiple compounds, including Isoamyl isobutyrate and Thelephantin K. These compounds all ultimately target CCRF-HSB-2, indicating a potential pathway where Phomalide may influence the cell line through its interaction with SNU-387. The shared target of these compounds with CCRF-HSB-2 suggests a possible mechanism of action involving receptor engagement or signaling pathways. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of SNU-387 as a central mediator in the interaction between Phomalide and CCRF-HSB-2, potentially through a common downstream effect on the cell line.",
